WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:12.880
Vinnie and Mandy stood on the lawn with their parents.

2
00:00:12.881 --> 00:00:16.476
They were all looking at their house.

3
00:00:16.477 --> 00:00:21.135
"Just a few more things we'll do," Dad said proudly.

4
00:00:21.136 --> 00:00:23.875
"Then our home will be perfect."

5
00:00:23.876 --> 00:00:28.084
"Today we're going to clean that attic," said Mom.

6
00:00:28.085 --> 00:00:32.411
"Yep, it's filled with junk," Dad said firmly.

7
00:00:32.412 --> 00:00:36.802
Speechless, Mandy poked her brother hard.

8
00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:40.068
"Ouch! We'll do it, Dad!"

9
00:00:40.069 --> 00:00:43.133
said Vinnie, rubbing his arm.

10
00:00:43.134 --> 00:00:47.476
"That's okay. I'll take care of it," Dad replied.

11
00:00:47.477 --> 00:00:50.066
He went into the house.

12
00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:53.741
"We have to get the album!" cried Vinnie.

13
00:00:53.742 --> 00:00:55.151
"Come on!"

14
00:00:55.152 --> 00:00:58.421
The children ran into the house.

15
00:00:58.422 --> 00:01:00.910
"Whoa! Where are you going?"

16
00:01:00.911 --> 00:01:04.669
Dad shouted as they ran past him.

17
00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:08.770
"We have to do something!" Vinnie cried.

18
00:01:08.771 --> 00:01:14.134
They raced up the attic stairs and slammed the door shut.

19
00:01:14.135 --> 00:01:18.607
"Vinnie! Grab the album!" cried Mandy.

20
00:01:18.608 --> 00:01:22.229
Vinnie opened the album to another page.

21
00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:26.950
"Mandy! Look!" Vinnie showed her the new photo.

22
00:01:26.951 --> 00:01:30.649
"We don't have time . . . ," Mandy began.

23
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:34.474
But her eyes were drawn to the beautiful photo.

24
00:01:34.475 --> 00:01:39.988
The old man was standing in front of a large group of Indians.

25
00:01:39.989 --> 00:01:42.874
They were standing in a circle.

26
00:01:42.875 --> 00:01:47.752
One Indian was holding something like a big belt.

27
00:01:47.753 --> 00:01:51.272
It glowed brightly.

28
00:01:51.273 --> 00:01:53.618
"What's going on up there?"

29
00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:57.299
Dad shouted angrily from below.

30
00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.405
Those were the last words the children heard.

31
00:02:01.406 --> 00:02:07.872
Their eyes closed and they fell down the dark tunnel.

32
00:02:07.873 --> 00:02:10.882
They landed on soft soil.

33
00:02:10.883 --> 00:02:16.678
"What's that smell?" Vinnie moaned.

34
00:02:16.679 --> 00:02:22.418
"Something's burning," replied Mandy.

35
00:02:22.419 --> 00:02:27.805
The children were in a village surrounded by a tall fence.

36
00:02:27.806 --> 00:02:35.618
Around them, long buildings with curved roofs were covered in bark and animal skins.

37
00:02:35.619 --> 00:02:39.739
A large fire burned in the middle of the village.

38
00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:45.421
People were throwing pieces of cloth into it.

39
00:02:45.422 --> 00:02:49.389
A young girl came out of a nearby house.

40
00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:53.009
She gasped loudly when she saw them.

41
00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:55.231
"How did you get in here?"

42
00:02:55.232 --> 00:02:58.146
she said, looking shocked.

43
00:02:58.147 --> 00:03:03.869
"Well, we just . . . ," said Mandy nervously.

44
00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:09.925
Like the girl, Vinnie and Mandy were wearing shirts made of animal skin.

45
00:03:09.926 --> 00:03:12.675
Vinnie wore pants underneath.

46
00:03:12.676 --> 00:03:17.951
Both Mandy and the girl wore a skirt.

47
00:03:17.952 --> 00:03:21.451
The girl stared angrily at Mandy.

48
00:03:21.452 --> 00:03:22.934
"You are white.

49
00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:26.580
You don't belong here," she said.

50
00:03:26.581 --> 00:03:31.427
Vinnie and Mandy did not know what to say.

51
00:03:31.428 --> 00:03:36.881
Just then, an old woman appeared from the same house.

52
00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:40.408
She looked at Vinnie and Mandy curiously.

53
00:03:40.409 --> 00:03:44.205
"Who are you?" she asked.

54
00:03:44.206 --> 00:03:48.538
The children introduced themselves.

55
00:03:48.539 --> 00:03:53.134
"Do you know where you are?" the woman asked.

56
00:03:53.135 --> 00:03:58.173
"Uh, not really," Vinnie replied truthfully.

57
00:03:58.174 --> 00:04:04.602
"This is the village of the Iroquois," said the old woman.

58
00:04:04.603 --> 00:04:09.408
"So go home!" the girl said in a mean way.

59
00:04:09.409 --> 00:04:16.406
"Onatah, it is the time of the Green Corn Festival," the woman said softly.

60
00:04:16.407 --> 00:04:20.954
"It is a time of thanksgiving and forgiveness."

61
00:04:20.955 --> 00:04:25.678
"I know, Grandmother," Onatah mumbled.

62
00:04:25.679 --> 00:04:30.947
Nodding, the old woman looked at Vinnie and Mandy again.

63
00:04:30.948 --> 00:04:33.427
"I am Clan Mother.

64
00:04:33.428 --> 00:04:41.791
The People of the Longhouse welcome you," she said.
